  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I already ran DRAGON on our methylation and expression layers and saved the partial-correlation matrix. Now I want CONDOR to find communities directly in that DRAGON matrix. The matrix is labeled and complete."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Now I want CONDOR to find communities directly in that DRAGON matrix.\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set. CONDOR gives: communities in one bipartite network, with regulator-side and gene-side memberships, by bipartite modularity. Each regulator's and gene's core score -- its share of its community's modularity -- to pick out each community's core nodes. DRAGON gives: one undirected partial-correlation network within and between two matched omics layers (any two, e.g. expression and methylation), across all samples. A p-value and a Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value for every edge (adjusted within each layer and across the layers), to filter edges by significance.\n\nI couldn't match this to a result any registered NetZoo workflow produces, so none is offered.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
